WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.360
July 2019.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.140
Europe is in the grip of a brutal drought.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.060
In the summer, parts of Europe recorded the
hottest heatwave they've experienced in

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:17.380
modern history. In Spain, temperatures climb
to 110°F.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.250
Consequence of this, a lot of bodies of water
began dropping at a rapid rate.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.990
Getting lower than they ever have.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.790
As waters recede and the Extremadura region
of the country.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.470
A ghost from the past is captured by
satellite cameras.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.940
Suddenly, seemingly out of nowhere, this ring
appears on the shoreline.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.450
An almost perfect circle.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.240
The ring shaped mound is around 120ft wide.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.710
It would have taken a significant amount of
effort to build something like this, so it

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.900
must have some important significance.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.630
The waters here form part of a reservoir
system.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.900
David Krueger looks at its history for
clues.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:22.020
This was formed as a result of a dam project
by the infamous General Francisco Franco.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:31.300
Fascist dictator Franco ruled Spain from
1939 to 1975.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.920
He's kind of Spain's answer to Adolf Hitler.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:41.220
He's a really brutal leader who ruled with
an iron fist for decades over Spain.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:47.000
Franco's reign is characterized by violent
oppression of the Spanish people.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:54.110
I wonder if this formation is something that
General Franco actually wanted to cover up by

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.190
flooding the area.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:04.870
Franco's attempt to seize power causes the
Spanish Civil War of 1936 to 1939 with

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.070
support from Hitler and Mussolini.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:11.860
His nationalist rebels defeat the
Republicans in a conflict that claims around

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.600
200,000 lives.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.630
The Spanish Civil War is particularly brutal
because now you're incorporating modern

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.740
bombers and tanks into combat, killing
thousands of soldiers.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.220
But also killing thousands of civilians.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:34.690
Following his victory, Franco embarks on a
campaign of violence and terror on those who

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.730
oppose his fascist ideals.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.910
Anybody's enemy of the state, you name it.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.370
Liberals, communists, Christians.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.140
Well, they're all targeted.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.200
They call it the white terror.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.340
Franco's death squads.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.100
Butcher Another 200,000 people.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:59.180
What happens in Spain is kind of medieval in
its brutality.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:07.700
You hear stories of death squads carrying
out mass public executions in bull rings and

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.020
grizzly tales of supporters supposedly
dancing in the victims blood.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.790
It's utterly barbaric.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.760
Around 140,000 of Franco's victims have never
been found.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.450
Buried in secret mass graves around the
country.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:28.120
People who were killed and ended up in these
mass graves are known today as Spain's

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:35.920
disappeared. Is it possible that what we see
here is an example of a mass grave site that

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.920
Franco covered up underneath the waters?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:45.260
Yet for Clint Giannoulas further aerial
images of the structure suggest it has a much

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.340
older origin.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.140
I believe it predates any industrial
technologies.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.830
You've got these stones that have been
carved and in placed vertically in a

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:02.420
formation that looks like Neolithic sites we
see across the UK and Europe.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:12.240
The Neolithic, also called the New Stone Age,
begins around 12,000 years ago.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.060
It sees mankind evolving from being hunter
gatherers to farming the land and forming

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.290
larger tribes.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.260
And at sites around Europe, mysterious
clusters of standing stones begin to appear.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.710
It's an era in which everything in the world
is changing dramatically, and people suddenly

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.010
have the ability to build large things on a
big scale.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:41.900
The exact purpose of these ancient edifices
is a mystery.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.190
Yet. Giannoulas thinks one section of the
Spanish structure could offer a clue.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.800
The interesting aspect for me is the
entryway.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:58.030
This is a classic shape that we see in sites
made of stone from the Neolithic and the

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.260
early Bronze Age.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:07.300
Giannoulas calculates that the entryway is
precisely aligned to the rising sun during

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.620
the summer solstice.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:17.260
What that means is on the summer solstice,
the first light of day would have come

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:20.410
through there and lit up the entire inside.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.260
And that makes it possible.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.540
Ritualistic or ceremonial site.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:33.040
Archaeologists think that the structure once
had a roof creating a prehistoric edifice

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.360
called a dolmen.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:41.590
Dolmens are ritual structures that are
related to death.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.040
We have to remember that with the earth on
top of it, this would have been a very dark

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.950
entryway into the underworld.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.380
Into a sacred space for communing with the
ancestors.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:04.320
Archaeological records offer grim clues as to
how the ancient peoples at this site communed

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.760
with their ancestors.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.610
When your relative dies, you might engage in
cannibalism.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:19.050
This is the idea that you are eating a piece
of your ancestor, that you are literally

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:23.820
taking a piece of them and incorporating it
into your body.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:31.650
Tests reveal that this ritual death chamber
dates back around 5000 years ago when pagans

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:36.270
worshipped at Stonehenge and pharaohs were
being interred in the Great Pyramids.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:44.570
But before archaeologists can investigate
further, the waters rise and its ancient

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.790
secrets are reclaimed once more.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:54.260
How lucky are we to get this brief glimpse
from space of this civilization that lived so

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.400
many years ago?

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.610
Who knows when we'll get to see it again?

